WEBVTT

00:01:30.352 --> 00:01:32.646
This is ALSUS?

00:01:33.188 --> 00:01:36.442
Yes, the multipurpose
surgical installation, ALSUS.

00:01:36.942 --> 00:01:40.654
However, the body
of the Matter has engulfed it.

00:01:42.656 --> 00:01:46.118
So, this giant blob of stuff is...

00:01:47.036 --> 00:01:51.624
That's right. It's your artificial body
that caused the Burst.

00:01:55.044 --> 00:01:55.961
Aiko!

00:01:57.588 --> 00:02:00.007
Aiko Tachibana! I'm sorry I took so long!

00:02:00.716 --> 00:02:02.259
It's me, Toshihide Yura!

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:05.304
The head's buried in the stomach!

00:02:05.804 --> 00:02:09.350
Her body turned to Matter,
and is looking for its own brain.

00:02:14.229 --> 00:02:17.107
I'll return your brains
to their proper bodies now.

00:02:17.483 --> 00:02:18.484
Can you hear me?

00:02:22.696 --> 00:02:23.530
Aiko!

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:27.701
Hey! Let me hear your voice again!

00:02:32.247 --> 00:02:33.624
How did this happen?

00:02:39.046 --> 00:02:40.506
We're surrounded!

00:02:54.561 --> 00:02:55.396
We made it!

00:02:55.562 --> 00:02:56.605
Holy shit!

00:02:57.815 --> 00:02:58.857
Is this her body?

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:01.026
Are you serious?

00:03:01.276 --> 00:03:02.820
Aiko, are you going to...?

00:03:04.113 --> 00:03:05.322
You are, aren't you?

00:03:07.199 --> 00:03:08.075
Yes.

00:03:11.328 --> 00:03:13.163
Thank you, everyone.

00:03:15.707 --> 00:03:18.043
If that's your decision, we accept it.

00:03:21.797 --> 00:03:22.715
Hurry, Kanzaki!

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:28.804
Thank you, Kanzaki.

00:03:30.097 --> 00:03:31.390
For creating me,

00:03:32.516 --> 00:03:35.811
and for finding the place
where I could be myself.

00:03:40.357 --> 00:03:41.191
Kanzaki?

00:03:43.527 --> 00:03:44.778
What are you doing?

00:03:47.448 --> 00:03:49.199
If this mission succeeded,

00:03:49.742 --> 00:03:54.288
I was going to end my own life
along with yours.

00:04:04.506 --> 00:04:05.883
An Anti-Cell Assembler.

00:04:06.467 --> 00:04:11.764
It was what he intended
to inject Aiko with to end the Burst.

00:04:12.639 --> 00:04:14.767
I don't want to kill you.

00:04:16.518 --> 00:04:18.061
You won't do the surgery?

00:04:18.812 --> 00:04:21.607
No, I promise the surgery
will be a success.

00:04:23.609 --> 00:04:28.197
I, Toshihide Yura, was going to
take responsibility for what I had done

00:04:29.031 --> 00:04:31.742
by returning everything to the way it was.

00:04:33.202 --> 00:04:35.120
That's why I brought you here.

00:04:36.872 --> 00:04:38.207
That was my intention.

00:04:38.791 --> 00:04:39.666
However,

00:04:40.918 --> 00:04:44.671
<i>you accepted the fact</i>
<i>that you're not the real Aiko Tachibana.</i>

00:04:45.422 --> 00:04:46.256
<i>Nonetheless,</i>

00:04:46.799 --> 00:04:50.969
<i>you searched for the best path</i>
<i>for the real Aiko and you, and took it.</i>

00:04:52.429 --> 00:04:54.973
That's no decision
a fake human could make.

00:04:56.308 --> 00:04:59.311
When I made you, you were not fake.

00:05:00.437 --> 00:05:04.107
From the moment you were born,
you were the real you.

00:05:04.566 --> 00:05:07.277
I cannot deny that you ever existed.

00:05:08.612 --> 00:05:10.989
I won't let you die.

00:05:13.867 --> 00:05:17.746
I myself will build a world
where you can live.

00:05:18.956 --> 00:05:21.959
That is the only way
to atone for what I've done.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:29.633
But, can you do that
while her body is Matter?

00:05:30.259 --> 00:05:31.134
I will!

00:05:32.094 --> 00:05:34.930
I'll share the burden
that you're about to bear.

00:05:35.681 --> 00:05:36.682
If you'll let me.

00:05:37.724 --> 00:05:38.850
Kanzaki...

00:05:39.726 --> 00:05:43.647
By my own hand,
I will return your body to the way it was.

00:05:55.993 --> 00:05:59.621
The original Aiko's consciousness
can't hold back the Matter.

00:06:00.372 --> 00:06:02.624
If she completely loses consciousness,

00:06:02.874 --> 00:06:05.836
even completing the surgery
won't get her back!

00:06:06.962 --> 00:06:10.591
<i>Aiko! If you don't hurry up</i>
<i>and come back to me,</i>

00:06:10.924 --> 00:06:13.385
<i>I'll never be able to wake up Yuzuha!</i>

00:06:14.678 --> 00:06:15.846
I won't let you!

00:06:16.597 --> 00:06:17.973
Can you hear me, Isazu?

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:22.185
Yuzuha's consciousness is seeking
to return to her body!

00:06:22.686 --> 00:06:26.106
If you cut the link
between her and her duplicate bodies--

00:06:26.189 --> 00:06:27.816
<i>Silence, Toshihide Yura!</i>

00:06:28.483 --> 00:06:31.695
I know more about Yuzuha than anyone else!

00:06:31.778 --> 00:06:33.155
PULSE
BLOOD PRESSURE

00:06:35.574 --> 00:06:37.576
It won't be long now, Yuzuha.

00:07:24.331 --> 00:07:25.457
Gummi!

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:27.668
When the Matter attacked you before,

00:07:27.751 --> 00:07:29.836
Gummi surrounded and protected you.

00:07:31.088 --> 00:07:32.381
-Don't worry.
-Okay.

00:07:33.507 --> 00:07:34.675
I'm closing the capsule.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:40.097
The next time we meet,
I'll be in the Matter, right?

00:07:41.139 --> 00:07:43.642
Don't worry. I swear to protect you.

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:50.667
<i>Those are...</i>

00:08:50.917 --> 00:08:54.129
<i>Yuzuha's duplicate bodies.</i>
<i>They didn't turn to Matter!</i>

00:08:54.463 --> 00:08:58.800
Yuzuha, let me borrow your sisters
for a while.

00:08:59.718 --> 00:09:02.304
Okay, I'll link to you now, my daughters.

00:09:03.263 --> 00:09:05.766
Become one with my mind.

00:09:07.809 --> 00:09:08.769
<i>Go to her.</i>

00:09:10.228 --> 00:09:11.688
<i>Go to Aiko.</i>

00:09:14.608 --> 00:09:16.610
Someone, help us!

00:09:23.992 --> 00:09:26.078
What? They stopped moving.

00:09:30.332 --> 00:09:31.541
-Look!
-Human forms!

00:09:31.625 --> 00:09:32.501
They're different!

00:09:36.588 --> 00:09:39.382
Those aren't human forms. They're humans!

00:09:40.217 --> 00:09:42.219
They're Yuzuha's duplicate bodies.

00:09:42.385 --> 00:09:44.638
Were they turned to Matter on purpose?

00:09:45.055 --> 00:09:46.973
Dammit, Isazu!

00:09:47.474 --> 00:09:49.142
Is it okay to shoot these?

00:09:49.726 --> 00:09:52.312
Yes!
Those duplicate aren't conscious.

00:09:52.687 --> 00:09:58.110
<i>Yuzuha, I swear I will bring you back.</i>

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:04.116
Commencing brain transfer surgery.

00:10:04.991 --> 00:10:05.992
A keyhole?

00:10:06.201 --> 00:10:08.745
<i>The lock on Yuzuha's room</i>
<i>isn't electronic.</i>

00:10:09.204 --> 00:10:10.914
<i>I can't hack it open.</i>

00:10:12.666 --> 00:10:15.210
We'll need someone
from the medical staff.

00:10:18.463 --> 00:10:19.297
Takehara!

00:10:20.048 --> 00:10:22.467
Dr. Kurose...

00:10:22.843 --> 00:10:24.761
<i>Removing hair and scalp.</i>

00:10:27.055 --> 00:10:29.516
<i>Yuzuha...</i>

00:10:29.599 --> 00:10:31.726
<i>Please stop, Dad!</i>

00:10:32.018 --> 00:10:34.938
<i>Don't worry. It won't be long now.</i>

00:10:35.647 --> 00:10:37.107
They're entering Aiko!

00:10:37.649 --> 00:10:39.317
Are they attacking her body?

00:10:39.776 --> 00:10:40.902
I'm out of bullets!

00:10:46.741 --> 00:10:47.576
This is bad!

00:10:48.118 --> 00:10:48.952
Isazu!

00:10:50.245 --> 00:10:51.663
How dare you!

00:10:52.455 --> 00:10:53.748
Stop it, Isazu!

00:10:54.082 --> 00:10:55.083
<i>How's this?</i>

00:10:56.001 --> 00:10:59.129
<i>If you can't return the duplicate brain</i>
<i>to this body,</i>

00:10:59.212 --> 00:11:02.132
<i>you'll never accomplish your objective!</i>

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:04.759
Damn you, Isazu!

00:11:04.885 --> 00:11:06.720
<i>It's not too late to turn back.</i>

00:11:06.928 --> 00:11:10.181
<i>Give Aiko to me as she is now!</i>

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:12.851
<i>Softening the skull.</i>

00:11:16.187 --> 00:11:18.523
Why are you here, Dr. Kurose?

00:11:19.858 --> 00:11:21.568
I want to save Yuzuha.

00:11:22.277 --> 00:11:23.111
What?

00:11:33.788 --> 00:11:37.042
<i>I can see it now! This is amazing!</i>

00:11:42.172 --> 00:11:44.883
He's controlling the duplicate body! Damn!

00:11:45.383 --> 00:11:48.470
Everyone! Fire at the head of that thing!

00:11:48.678 --> 00:11:49.638
-Wilco!
-Wilco!

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:56.519
<i>Skull opened.</i>

00:11:56.937 --> 00:11:59.147
<i>Cell Assembler Two hemostasis normal.</i>

00:12:00.649 --> 00:12:05.153
<i>Now for the removal of the brain,</i>
<i>medulla, and eyes by Cell Assembler Three.</i>

00:12:06.655 --> 00:12:08.448
Yuzuha will wake up...

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:11.534
if we cut her link
to the duplicate bodies?

00:12:13.244 --> 00:12:14.079
Yes.

00:12:19.209 --> 00:12:21.086
CONNECTING

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:25.840
I can't shoot Aiko's body!

00:12:29.344 --> 00:12:30.178
Kaede!

00:12:34.099 --> 00:12:34.933
Aiko!

00:12:36.434 --> 00:12:39.104
<i>I'll move! I'm going to move!</i>

00:12:39.187 --> 00:12:41.272
<i>My body can go anywhere!</i>

00:12:47.737 --> 00:12:48.571
Shit!

00:12:53.243 --> 00:12:54.077
Sagami!

00:12:56.246 --> 00:12:57.080
Sagami!

00:13:00.417 --> 00:13:01.918
<i>Cranial nerves extracted.</i>

00:13:03.003 --> 00:13:05.964
<i>Brain waves normal. Body vitals stable.</i>

00:13:10.969 --> 00:13:11.803
Damn it!

00:13:12.345 --> 00:13:14.806
Forget about me! Protect Kanzaki!

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:23.064
Damn it!

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:26.359
<i>The human body is such an inconvenience!</i>

00:13:29.571 --> 00:13:32.365
<i>The brain is properly affixed</i>
<i>within the skull.</i>

00:13:32.657 --> 00:13:35.869
<i>Commencing connection</i>
<i>of nervous and vascular systems.</i>

00:13:36.411 --> 00:13:38.204
<i>It's so powerless!</i>

00:13:41.207 --> 00:13:43.626
That's the Anti-Cell Assembler!

00:13:44.127 --> 00:13:48.173
But that vial isn't for shooting.
We can't fire it with a gun!

00:13:49.758 --> 00:13:50.717
In that case...

00:13:59.267 --> 00:14:00.935
Kaede! Shoot into here!

00:14:02.479 --> 00:14:05.482
Disperse the Anti-Cell Assembler
inside its body!

00:14:05.732 --> 00:14:06.566
-What?
-What?

00:14:06.733 --> 00:14:08.443
But, if I do that...

00:14:08.943 --> 00:14:11.738
You know this isn't my real arm!

00:14:19.954 --> 00:14:21.373
-Here it goes!
-Do it!

00:14:24.459 --> 00:14:25.377
Keep it up!

00:14:35.512 --> 00:14:38.598
<i>Yuzuha...</i>

00:14:39.099 --> 00:14:42.352
<i>Yuzuha...</i>

00:14:43.436 --> 00:14:44.604
Did we do it?

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:51.111
<i>Dad? What's wrong? Dad?</i>

00:14:51.694 --> 00:14:52.695
<i>Dad!</i>

00:15:00.078 --> 00:15:00.912
Yuzuha!

00:15:11.131 --> 00:15:12.799
<i>Confirming neural fusion.</i>

00:15:14.175 --> 00:15:17.720
<i>Skull closed. Scalp and hair regenerated.</i>

00:15:17.804 --> 00:15:20.974
DELINKING SUCCESSFUL

00:15:24.018 --> 00:15:27.897
The link to the duplicate bodies
is severed. Vitals are normal.

00:15:28.857 --> 00:15:29.899
Yuzuha?

00:15:38.241 --> 00:15:39.784
Surgery complete.

00:16:01.556 --> 00:16:02.390
Is it over?

00:16:03.349 --> 00:16:06.394
Have both Aiko and I been returned

00:16:07.312 --> 00:16:09.772
to our own bodies?

00:16:11.441 --> 00:16:12.275
Yes.

00:16:13.693 --> 00:16:14.694
Thank goodness.

00:16:25.497 --> 00:16:29.542
<i>I've just released Mom and Ryota</i>
<i>from the cocoon.</i>

00:16:30.627 --> 00:16:32.337
Someone go help them.

00:16:34.589 --> 00:16:37.759
Can someone see to them?
I'll share their position.

00:16:38.259 --> 00:16:39.928
Roger! Kaede.

00:16:40.094 --> 00:16:41.137
Okay!

00:16:52.398 --> 00:16:53.358
Dr. Yura.

00:16:54.275 --> 00:16:57.070
Am I back to normal?

00:16:57.445 --> 00:16:58.279
Yes.

00:16:59.822 --> 00:17:02.450
Is that really the other Aiko?

00:17:05.119 --> 00:17:06.204
Nice to meet you.

00:17:09.123 --> 00:17:11.167
Doctor, what about the other girl?

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:18.091
Thank goodness.

00:17:19.092 --> 00:17:20.134
You're back.

00:17:30.061 --> 00:17:32.021
Aiko!

00:17:32.814 --> 00:17:35.275
Hey! Answer! Please!

00:17:35.358 --> 00:17:36.609
Aiko!

00:17:38.611 --> 00:17:39.445
Tachibana!

00:17:39.779 --> 00:17:41.573
Come on!

00:17:42.574 --> 00:17:43.950
It didn't work?

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:46.035
She came all this way...

00:17:47.495 --> 00:17:48.329
Aiko...

00:17:49.455 --> 00:17:51.541
Why?

00:17:53.042 --> 00:17:56.129
You did it for Mom, for Ryota,

00:17:56.879 --> 00:17:57.964
for me...

00:17:59.132 --> 00:18:00.508
You did so much for us.

00:18:03.261 --> 00:18:04.095
Aiko...

00:18:28.911 --> 00:18:29.746
What's that?

00:18:35.293 --> 00:18:37.462
Is that Matter, too?

00:18:55.229 --> 00:18:56.064
Aiko?

00:18:58.691 --> 00:19:00.443
What? Why are you...

00:19:01.694 --> 00:19:03.196
What? I'm...

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:11.704
Gummi?

00:19:11.913 --> 00:19:15.333
Her body was regenerated? But how?

00:19:16.542 --> 00:19:19.128
Did Gummi have a copy of Aiko's body data?

00:19:22.173 --> 00:19:24.801
I'm... I'm...

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:27.095
I'm not dreaming?

00:19:30.056 --> 00:19:30.890
That's right.

00:19:34.727 --> 00:19:35.561
It hurts!

00:19:36.229 --> 00:19:37.230
It's not a dream!

00:19:37.814 --> 00:19:38.815
Thank goodness.

00:19:45.071 --> 00:19:47.198
I'm so happy.

00:19:48.908 --> 00:19:50.034
I can't believe it.

00:19:50.952 --> 00:19:52.954
Her dad was the one who saved her.

00:19:57.542 --> 00:19:58.626
Shiraishi.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:08.261
But, why?

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:12.014
I'll explain everything to Mom and Ryota.

00:20:12.432 --> 00:20:13.641
They'll understand.

00:20:14.434 --> 00:20:16.811
I want the four of us to live together.

00:20:17.395 --> 00:20:20.356
No. I want to return everything to normal.

00:20:20.982 --> 00:20:25.069
Since you had to go through so much,
losing your father,

00:20:25.403 --> 00:20:26.362
and the Burst,

00:20:26.988 --> 00:20:32.326
I want you, Mom, and Ryota
to live a peaceful life together.

00:20:32.744 --> 00:20:33.578
But...

00:20:33.745 --> 00:20:34.579
Please.

00:20:34.662 --> 00:20:35.496
But!

00:20:36.247 --> 00:20:39.000
I think you understand how I feel.

00:20:41.002 --> 00:20:44.255
That makes me happy.
Thank you, Aiko.

00:20:45.256 --> 00:20:47.383
Then, you can at least...

00:20:51.804 --> 00:20:53.389
-Thank you.
-Thanks!

00:20:53.598 --> 00:20:54.932
Mom! Ryota!

00:20:55.892 --> 00:20:57.477
-Aiko!
-Aiko!

00:20:58.686 --> 00:21:00.062
Are you two all right?

00:21:00.354 --> 00:21:02.148
I feel a little lightheaded.

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:04.567
I was so worried. Are you okay?

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:05.485
Yes.

00:21:06.068 --> 00:21:07.862
Really? Thank goodness.

00:21:08.613 --> 00:21:10.114
Thank you, Aiko.

00:21:10.531 --> 00:21:11.449
I'm hungry.

00:21:12.533 --> 00:21:14.619
They'll get you to a hospital soon.

00:21:15.119 --> 00:21:18.456
Get checked out, eat something,
and get some sleep.

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:21.167
I only wish that your father

00:21:22.001 --> 00:21:24.128
could see you doing so well.

00:21:25.004 --> 00:21:25.838
Yes.

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:28.716
Dad protected me a lot, too.

00:21:30.092 --> 00:21:34.388
Oh, that's right. I need to say thank you
to everyone that came with you.

00:21:35.139 --> 00:21:38.059
Who are those guys? They're totally cool!

00:21:38.434 --> 00:21:40.269
They came with me to save you.

00:21:40.937 --> 00:21:42.188
They're my friends.

00:21:42.438 --> 00:21:45.733
Your friends? No way!
You're awesome, Aiko!

00:21:51.113 --> 00:21:51.948
Aiko?

00:21:52.031 --> 00:21:52.865
Aiko?

00:21:55.076 --> 00:21:57.745
I'm so glad you're both okay.

00:21:58.955 --> 00:22:01.749
Thank goodness you're alive.

00:22:08.506 --> 00:22:10.132
I'm going to go change.

00:22:28.985 --> 00:22:30.778
Where will you go after this?

00:22:31.487 --> 00:22:33.155
I'll have to think about it.

00:22:34.657 --> 00:22:38.828
I know there is a world
where you can exist. I'm sure of it.

00:22:40.288 --> 00:22:41.330
If there isn't...

00:22:42.415 --> 00:22:43.457
I'll make it.

00:22:45.126 --> 00:22:45.960
Okay.

00:23:04.478 --> 00:23:07.607
Shiraishi, thank you for everything.

00:23:08.399 --> 00:23:09.275
Aiko...

00:23:33.966 --> 00:23:36.052
-Crystallized and collapsed?
-What?

00:23:36.469 --> 00:23:39.305
The Matter around Primary Point
has collapsed.

00:23:40.348 --> 00:23:43.517
-I'm here to pick you up, Director.
-The whole thing?

00:23:51.692 --> 00:23:52.693
Dad...

00:23:54.195 --> 00:23:55.279
Dad?

00:24:02.828 --> 00:24:04.080
We're together again.

00:24:04.205 --> 00:24:07.833
How many times have you
and I been in the same class?

00:24:10.002 --> 00:24:12.963
Hey, Ryota! Lend us a hand!

00:24:13.089 --> 00:24:14.757
It hurts!

00:24:14.840 --> 00:24:15.758
Are you okay?

00:24:16.133 --> 00:24:17.426
It's fine. I'm fine.

00:24:17.843 --> 00:24:19.595
Watch what you're doing.

00:24:20.096 --> 00:24:21.347
Go on. Wash it.

00:24:21.430 --> 00:24:22.974
My sister is such a klutz!

00:24:23.224 --> 00:24:25.643
Ryota! Don't leave your ball there!

00:24:28.646 --> 00:24:31.399
First, expand these two equations.

00:24:33.526 --> 00:24:34.360
Yuzuha!

00:24:35.194 --> 00:24:36.904
It's a gift from Dr. Yura.

00:24:37.780 --> 00:24:40.825
<i>You're fine.</i>
<i>Your mind and body are normal.</i>

00:24:41.033 --> 00:24:43.202
<i>Your next checkup will be...</i>

00:24:43.285 --> 00:24:46.914
<i>Summer vacation.</i>
<i>It has been a year since it all happened.</i>

00:24:47.289 --> 00:24:48.499
<i>That's right.</i>

00:24:49.125 --> 00:24:52.545
<i>I really want to meet her again,</i>
<i>and everyone else.</i>

00:24:53.254 --> 00:24:54.630
<i>The time will come.</i>

00:24:55.297 --> 00:24:57.591
<i>Yes, when the time comes.</i>

00:24:59.719 --> 00:25:02.346
I'm here. Let's go.

00:25:03.305 --> 00:25:08.519
<i>This is another day for me</i>
<i>to make memories that are all my own.</i>

00:25:09.186 --> 00:25:10.521
YUBARI SHIMIZUSAWA HIGH

00:25:10.604 --> 00:25:12.356
<i>We have a new transfer student.</i>

00:25:25.202 --> 00:25:27.830
It's nice to meet you. My name is...

00:25:28.456 --> 00:25:30.541
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
